- op: discuss  # e61f
  at: '2026-09-01T21:30:22Z'  # e61f
  by: agent  # e61f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e61f
  clock: 3  # e61f
  nonce: e61f  # e61f
  message: "DONE in PR #693, merged to dev as fd8a7f39ef. 12,476 tests, 100% coverage, mypy\nratchet clean.\n\nTHE ITEM'S OWN DONE CRITERION, MEASURED WITH A CONTROL RATHER THAN ASSERTED:\n\"a new undeclared multi-value field on IoPrimitive fails CI\".\n  clean tree                                 gate exit 0\n  probe_field: str planted on IoPrimitive    gate exit 1, offender named\n  DEFAULT_CORE_FILES                         3 files (ir, datamodels, io_boundary)\n  find_field_drift over all scoped files     none\nThe first run of this control reported \"exit=0\" because the pipeline's status\nwas GREP's, not the script's. Re-measured cleanly; recording that because the\nwrong number looked exactly like a passing gate.\n\nTHE FIRST STEP THE ITEM DEMANDED WAS RIGHT TO DEMAND. Report-only mode before\ntouching anything found 20 undeclared fields across SEVEN dataclasses, not\nIoPrimitive's six: IoBoundaryCatalog, DefaultOverlay, ModeArgument, IoChain,\nBoundaryMapEntry, FirstPartyModuleGrammar.\n\nEACH FIELD READ AND CLASSIFIED INDIVIDUALLY, none bulk-stamped.\n  io-boundary   IoPrimitive.boundary, IoChain.boundary, BoundaryMapEntry.boundary\n  module-key    IoPrimitive.module\n  language      IoBoundaryCatalog, DefaultOverlay, FirstPartyModuleGrammar\n  identity      IoChain.io_edge_src, io_edge_dst\n  bounded-enum  IoPrimitive.kind, IoPrimitive.boundary_ruling,\n                IoBoundaryCatalog.status, IoChain.dst_tier_name\n  free-text     the rest, with justifications CHECKED AGAINST THE CODE --\n                IoPrimitive.name is free-text because _by_short[p.name] uses it\n                whole as a dict key and never decomposes it, which was verified\n                rather than assumed. A free-text justification that is not true\n                is the exact defect ADR-0051 removed, and the lint cannot tell\n                the difference because it only requires it to be PRESENT.\n\nFOUND WHILE DECLARING: IoBoundaryCatalog.status's THIRD value was undocumented.\nCalling it a bounded enum required listing the values, which surfaced that\n`unsupported` -- the status of a catalogue that does not exist (WI-gofah), which\na YAML may not declare -- appeared nowhere in the class docstring beside\nprovenance_declared and in_progress. Now documented with the reason it is\nproducer-only.\n\nTWO NON-VACUITY TESTS, because a path in DEFAULT_CORE_FILES that the AST walker\ncannot parse yields zero offenders and is indistinguishable from a clean file:\none asserts the walker actually yields IoPrimitive's fields, one asserts the two\nspecific axis names (a regression to free-text would otherwise still pass).\n\nKNOWN GAP, DISCLOSED RATHER THAN LEFT TO BE FOUND. .githooks/pre-commit fires\nthis check on ^packages/.*/src/.*/(ir|datamodels)\\.py$, so staging ONLY\nio_boundary.py skips it -- demonstrated by this very commit, whose hook output\nreads \"Multi-value field axis declaration... skipped\" while staging a file that\nis now in scope. CI is unaffected: test_live_tree_passes runs find_field_drift\nover all three files regardless of staging, which is why the item's DONE\ncriterion is met. Only the local fast-feedback path is narrower than the\nconstant it serves. The one-line regex fix and the matching AGENTS.md sentence\n(\"in ir.py or datamodels.py\") are governance-file edits held for approval rather\nthan bundled. The PLAYBOOK, which is not a governance file, is updated here.\n\nTHE GENERALISABLE LESSON, written into the playbook: THE SCOPE OF\nDEFAULT_CORE_FILES IS THE SCOPE OF THE DISCIPLINE. A dataclass carrying a\nvocabulary and not named there is unlinted by construction, however carefully\nits own module is written -- so when declaring an axis, ask where BOTH halves of\nthe field live before assuming the lint covers it.\n\nINV-tafig can now close: its remaining blocker was IoPrimitive.boundary carrying\nno axis comment, which this supplies."  # e61f
